MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Establishes the architectural baseline for Boop OS before any feature code.
No application yet: this commit defines what gets built and under which rules.

Analysis
- Reviews the V0 spec and records 11 inconsistencies with the resolution
  adopted for each (journey stages mixing status and stage, versionable
  fields placed on the content item, email needed in phase 5 but scheduled
  for 16, onboarding file uploads preceding the files phase, …)
- Records 15 risks with mitigations, and 12 open decisions each with an
  assumed default and the phase by which it must be settled

Architecture
- Modular monolith: Next.js App Router + Supabase, server-first data access
- Layered: UI → entrypoints → workflows → policy → repository → database
- Two authorization layers: application checks and RLS, neither sufficient alone
- Journeys as typed templates in code; stages materialized per project
- Content and strategy versioned; approval binds to the version, never the item

Data model
- 21 tables for V0, split by phase; 9 tables from the spec deliberately deferred
  with the trigger that would bring each one back
- Tenant columns derived by trigger and immutable; append-only activity log
  carrying a visibility flag from the first migration

Security
- Threat model, RLS built on security-definer helpers in a non-exposed schema,
  private storage with two-step signed uploads, service-role confinement,
  known gaps stated rather than glossed over

Documentation
- CLAUDE.md, 10 docs, 15 ADRs, 5 enforcement rule sets
- docs/ holds the reasoning, .claude/rules/ holds the obligations, no duplication

