Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 03:31:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/31] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20phase=201=20=E2=80=94=20technical?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20foundation?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turns the architecture-only repository into a running application. No product
features: no database, no auth, no domain logic. Just a foundation the next
phases can build on without rework.

Stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router, Server Components by default) + React 19
- TypeScript 5.9 strict, plus noUncheckedIndexedAccess,
  exactOptionalPropertyTypes and verbatimModuleSyntax
- Tailwind 4 with tokens as CSS variables, Zod 4, Vitest 4 + Testing Library
- pnpm 10 and Node 22 pinned; npm and yarn fail via engine-strict

Routes
- / renders the foundation page, and in development only, which integrations
  are configured — booleans, never values
- /portal and /admin get independent layouts so the visual phase can diverge
  one without touching the other
- /app redirects to /portal: the briefing named the route /app, phase 0
  documented /portal, and an alias keeps both without a duplicate page

Environment
- One module owns process.env; a lint rule forbids reading it anywhere else
- Two categories: validated at boot (two variables, both with dev defaults)
  versus validated when an integration is actually used, so dev and build run
  with an empty .env.local through phase 17

Security baseline
- Six response headers, verified against a production build; portal and admin
  respond private, no-store; framework version not advertised
- Service role confined to one file that imports server-only
- console confined to the logger, which redacts sensitive keys at any depth
- CSP deliberately deferred to phase 19: a useful policy needs per-request
  nonces, and unsafe-inline now would only look like protection
- robots disallows everything — the product is entirely authenticated

Error handling
- Error boundaries at root, portal and admin, plus a global-error that cannot
  depend on the layout, and a 404 phrased so it does not distinguish a missing
  resource from a forbidden one — the wording phase 4 needs

Quality
- pnpm check runs typecheck, lint, format and tests; CI adds the build
- 23 tests: env behaviour with integrations absent, logger redaction,
  component accessibility, and one asserting no env value reaches the HTML
- Two lint exceptions, both narrow and commented: tests may touch process.env,
  and next.config may declare async without await

Also
- ADR-0016 records the toolchain, including staying one line behind latest on
  TypeScript and ESLint because typescript-eslint and eslint-config-next do
  not support the newest releases yet
- ADR-0017 records the environment split
- Documentation updated: npm to pnpm throughout, headers and env rules folded
  into security, staged CI in deployment, visual system inserted as phase 1.5
  rather than renumbering eighteen phases and their cross-references

