Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

@supabase/ssr, @supabase/supabase-js and server-only are imported by
src/lib/supabase/{server,admin}.ts — application code, not tooling. They were
installed with -D in phase 1, which would have broken a production install the
moment phase 3 started importing those modules.

Moved to dependencies. No version changed: the lockfile diff is the same nine
lines relocated between blocks, with identical specifiers and resolutions.
Verified with an isolated `pnpm install --prod --frozen-lockfile`, which now
resolves all seven runtime packages.

Audited the rest of the manifest: every other devDependency is tooling
(tailwind and its postcss plugin compile at build and emit plain CSS; types are
erased; eslint, prettier, vitest and testing-library never ship), and every
declared package is referenced by code or config — @testing-library/dom is a
required peer of @testing-library/react, and prettier-plugin-tailwindcss is
wired in .prettierrc.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GNCydr15SRkdUC4T2eACE5
---
 package.json   |  6 +++---
 pnpm-lock.yaml | 18 +++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

