From 34cbb6414f7a2133a2658a7a9a15c7b5e31869ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:14:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/31] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20phase=201.5=20=E2=80=94=20Boop=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?visual=20system=20and=20navigable=20prototype?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turns the technical foundation into the digital product: a client portal that
reads as Boop with the logo removed. Eleven screens, fictional data, nothing
persisted.

Brand reading
The logo is a pair of eyes — the two o's of "boop". The institutional deck is
entirely quarry, marble and sculpture, with "we don't build generic things" set
over rows of identical blocks: the market mass-produces, Boop carves. Their own
stated principle is "strategy before aesthetics".

That gives the concept: an open workshop. The product's promise — knowing
exactly what is happening — is already the brand's symbol, so the eyes are not
decoration. They look at the client precisely when something needs them, and at
the stage currently being worked.

Colour, taken from the assets rather than invented
#00C2FF, #0B1B2C, #FFFDF5 and #7AD7F4 come from the brand SVGs; the
atmospheric slate and bone come from sampling the deck. The vivid blue fails as
text on light (2.03:1) and fails under white, so the primary action is blue with
navy text at 8.42:1 — which is exactly what the logo does. The constraint became
the signature, and a test reads globals.css so it cannot silently regress.

What makes it read as Boop without the mark
Editorial slabs instead of cards; warm off-white instead of white, so the screen
reads as printed; Poppins Bold at poster scale against 11px tracked-out metadata;
near-square corners; no shadow anywhere. The journey is a row of carved blocks,
never a percentage.

Architecture
Screens talk to src/lib/data, never to src/mocks. Every function there is async
and takes a projectId, so swapping mocks for Supabase in phase 5 changes no
screen, and requireProjectAccess already has its seat. Content visibility is
filtered with the same rule RLS will enforce, so drafts and backlog never reach
the portal even in the prototype.

Dependencies: one added, tailwind-merge, on the trigger phase 1 wrote down. No
Radix, no shadcn, no icon library, no Framer Motion — native <dialog> and CSS
keyframes covered it (ADR-0018).

Visual QA found and fixed real defects
Calendar dates rendered a day early (UTC parsed, São Paulo formatted); max-w in
ch on a wrapper resolved against the wrong font size; secondary text on the
slate slab failed contrast; the brand mark stretched inside a flex column;
thumbnail hooks overflowed a 64px box; a 9:16 preview grew past 1600px on
tablet; the status mark contradicted the approval panel after approving.
Zero horizontal overflow at 375, 430, 768, 1024 and 1440.

Docs: design-direction, design-system and motion; ADR-0018; architecture,
roadmap, README, CLAUDE.md and the frontend rules updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
