From 2d7fdfbe599853aaa724ddef5d2288788bc7fbc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:15:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] chore(db): align migration filenames with the staging
 ledger
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ledger is the record of what actually ran; the filename is just a label.
When they disagree, the next person to run `supabase db push` learns it the
expensive way.

`apply_migration` over MCP stamps its own version at apply time and ignores the
version in the filename I chose. Both phase 5 migrations drifted, not just the
one that was spotted:

  repo 20260902160001_people_administration_boundaries.sql → ledger 20260902101850
  repo 20260902170001_immutable_authorship.sql            → ledger 20260902165421

Renamed to match. Relative order is preserved (092655 < 101850 < 165421), so a
local rebuild applies them in the same sequence as before, and the doc
references that named the old files were updated with them.

Nothing was reapplied, no SQL body changed, no schema touched: the two files are
byte-identical under a different name, and git records them as pure renames.
Verified by rebuilding the local database from the renamed files and comparing —
the fingerprint still matches staging across all nine parts, and the QA data
(one client, two people, five events) is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
