From d4a05e88c9915dd53341095f3975072e563204de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:40:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] fix(auth): name the invite-callback failure instead of
 blaming the link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The hosted QA clicked an invite link and got "esse link não funciona mais".
Requesting an ordinary Magic Link on that same screen worked. The staging edge
logs settled it without guessing:

  19:30:45  /auth/v1/verify?token=e4cf5fad…&type=invite         → 303
  19:31:23  /auth/v1/verify?token=pkce_ddef0559…&type=magiclink → 303
  19:31:24  POST /auth/v1/token?grant_type=pkce                 → 200

The invite token carries no `pkce_` prefix — a link born on the server has no
code challenge — and nothing follows it. No token exchange. GoTrue returned the
session in the URL fragment, and a fragment never reaches the server, so the
callback landed with an empty query and failed closed.

Root cause is configuration: the Supabase "Invite user" template is still the
default `{{ .ConfirmationURL }}`, routing through /auth/v1/verify instead of
carrying `{{ .TokenHash }}` to our callback. It is the manual step already
recorded in deployment.md as the one that breaks silently, and it had not been
applied. The dashboard is not touched here — the exact snippet goes to the
operator.

So the callback code needed no functional change, and gets none: both doors
still work exactly as before, and the token_hash → verifyOtp path already had
tests. What it lacked was the ability to describe its own failure. A request
arriving with no parameters at all has one likely cause in this system, and now
says so in the log rather than sending the next person to hunt for an expired
token. The user-facing message is unchanged: for whoever clicked, both cases are
still "ask for a new link".

Three regression cases pin the fail-closed shapes: no parameters at all, a bare
`?type=` with no token_hash, and Supabase's own `?error=` winning over the
generic branch.

628 to 631 tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RFdNJdA7V3tH1qhUk2cMa2
